# Witness (step 21.6): a body is a Structure. The DATA of an executable Structure is its parent; a callable (fn)
# has its own data and its own way of call, and a call of it is written in the body of the case. The entry
# Case\run on a callable is refused: answer 3, nothing ran (Case\seen stays 0).
Case:
    int: seen 0
    fn: run () int
        data\seen := 5
        return: 0
